# Copy and typography

- Never use em dashes (U+2014) in user-facing copy, comments, docs, or commit messages. Prefer periods, commas, colons, or parentheses.
- Empty table/UI placeholders may use a single em dash character only when meaning "no value".
- Fonts: IBM Plex Sans for UI and headlines (`font-sans` / `font-display`), IBM Plex Mono (`font-mono`).
- Do not introduce DM Sans, Inter, Roboto, Arial, Geist, Source Serif display pairing, or system-ui as the primary brand face.
- Do not use gradient `bg-clip-text` / transparent headline text.
- Marketing H1 should stay around `text-3xl sm:text-4xl`, not giant `text-5xl` stacks. App page titles stay about `text-2xl`.
- Avoid em dashes, en dashes, and arrow glyphs (→) in marketing copy. Prefer periods or commas.
